<title>ITALY: Ciampi signs Italy pension fund regulations - source.</title>
<headline>Ciampi signs Italy pension fund regulations - source.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi has signed regulations allowing pension funds to operate, a government source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The source gave no further details.</p>
<p>Reforms to the Italian pension sector last year removed obstacles to the launch of private pension funds and the government has been working on measures to provide a regulatory framework for their management.</p>
<p>Many trade unions, foreign companies, banks and insurance groups have expressed interest in entering the market.</p>
</text>
